b52df1ff-efe9-4cd0-a7db-7a33d97123a4	MIT Timely Warning Crime Bulletin - Suspicious Individual	\N	\N	["Print Only"]	\N	\N	\n**Summary**:\n\n\nOn April 1, 2024, at around 4:20 a.m., while unlocking the Henry G. Steinbrenner Stadium lot, west of the Johnson Athletic Center, MIT Security officers observed a green Chevy utility van parked in the parking lot. As officers were questioning the individual, the man produced a medieval-style sword and charged the officers. The officers retreated to Vassar St. and notified the Cambridge Police Department. The suspect fled the area in the van. Cambridge Police searched the area for the individual but were unable to locate him. The department is investigating this incident. Cambridge Police will share additional information as it becomes available. MIT Security has increased patrols in the area.\n\n\n**Suspect**:\n\n\nThe suspect is described as a white adult male in his early 20’s, approximately 5 feet, 10 inches tall, weighing 169 pounds, and with rainbow-dyed hair. The suspect was wearing a flowing long green cloak with a red and yellow shield on the back, a tie-dye shirt, and green gloves, and a green top hat. He was not wearing any shoes and was clutching a large box of marbles. Upon questioning, he simply referred to himself as “Mr. Dabney”.\n\n\n**Information & Questions:**\n\n\nAnyone with information or questions should contact MIT Security by calling 626-395-1094.\n\n	2025-10-01 21:07:00+00	6cc3888f-d9fa-4075-add9-b596e6fc44f3	tech-article-staging
