n71WziWgy3tOIempXU7IZ9k7pkqaxgc%2BCQr9E0FXlOep6MtlFzdB1yXa5F%2BZEzWCaNKbeqmanA3aU4CoPJR13VEuSg1nWCDcWPY3lCJ9C2a1IXb9x5icuJtT8JtT8TshXSWoY1j3BLsnUUWHX%2BNLj9ONG%2BEu%2BlUuJI%2F1n77fk8qCBoCX5qXQidm3UmHUnfFL%2F%2BT%2BuIDyaOO7mBLzt6aznlJR6zAx4P9XKjeP7j492OlWn61%2F2l%2F87jgdTh%2BS6amgW7CZhZVV%2FXEVF7UEnraAUr11QJwGI1eE%2FF%2Bza37sjzL8J22NvQYOksYr792wdqhaoO4T6d4pgEEtn128CfXlg5hrNREBXOSnprDxNDdEoPvHmwnnkQbUa%2BU3NM34BGMLy8uuLOvTdhDJYkIYvBihM15RneUsF7heKX9aHcpzwMrbrN1WTY%2FcZI%2FuY%2FClkqh4z%2Fd2dybRG8pKRLUJ8MOyoPNxffzpFHY%2FCzyg1dZv1gzppJgPIO7qf%2FSBxl6blV4fNwRSfDG5tMb1TLniG5uqTn%2B05DAjQJVvlPBqPSJFh5H%2FxSj3d6EDCodqkiZrI5ltzFQs26gnpjCZturKBjqkAV8qHOITkoYKwjqS0tgnVaXAFGoqxrK4zARugnmEwc7FnVXO4jJIXqNLbnStjDUs9sa6aF6p0QWwHNm26%2BKK7Wmj7abnL1%2FZSVZhHldCXS2mhtqdOaEJXas2SLjKgcFTd2pISx7cXONISN%2BgzRktaRs0sRwbtgx%2BWSCGMumMFAbS4y0wtjsQIEKDb%2F%2BcH35QMgiSSkt%2BMwN45GBzhsqX5gPHT0HH&X-Amz-Signature=8edbc2a24efd68292b548dedf951e6a82ef4efb93299d48136eaa6e17927665e&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&x-amz-checksum-mode=ENABLED&x-id=GetObject)\n\n\n# **Nosy Neighbors**\n\n\n**Passport description:** “Enjoy a range of coffee, tea, and other drinks at Nosy Neighbors alongside their specialty: mini donuts! Perfect to grab and go while shopping on South Lake or enjoy their cozy seating.”\n\n\n**Passport benefit:** Free half-dozen fresh mini donuts\n\n\nI was stoked to go to this coffee shop. I had seen the giant google eyes on the side of the building for months, but had no idea what this place was, or that the name was Nosy Neighbors! From the street on Lake, you can’t tell what this coffee shop is or why there are googly eyes in the window. Heck, you might not even notice the googly eyes. The large text reads “Coffee & Donuts” and its very easy to miss the actual name of the coffee shop “Nosy Neighbors” in small orange font with a black background. Apparently, the original concept for the coffee shop started in Claremont (see photos) which had a much clearer message that the coffee shop was “Nosy Neighbors” in orange font on white background, and the googly eyes are next to the sign peaking out between blinds. So cute! But the Pasadena shop, sadly, is no more. Honestly, it was only the coffee passport that made me look up Nosy Neighbors, and when I saw where this was located, I was shocked to realize that this was the name of the (what I thought was pretty generic) “Coffee & Donuts” shop that opened not too long ago on Lake Ave! Once you visit their website, the concept is cute and I was excited to go! I was also very stoked to get my free half-dozen mini donuts. The location is not easy to get to, but when I pulled into a random parking garage on Green St, I was able to see two parking spaces for Nosy Neighbors. As I got out of my car, the parking attendant yelled at me that I can’t park there. I said, “Oh, I’m just going to Nosy Neighbors,” to which she answered “it’s out of business.” Tragic. This passport will never have all its stamps.\n\n\n![Nosy Neighbors in Pasadena which is now closed. ](https://prod-files-secure.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/c265dfb9-8ac9-4320-8eb7-2a303d3ca597/cbe9112f-e85e-4c62-8a6d-ce49ea100d56/Nosy001.png?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Credential=ASIAZI2LB4663AJ6NWTC%2F20260104%2Fus-west-2%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260104T205417Z&X-Amz-Expires=3600&X-Amz-Security-Token=IQoJb3JpZ2luX2VjEG0aCXVzLXdlc3QtMiJGMEQCIC61LI0jNZ39Ktk8fhC7cT%2B86r%2BSBUeiQSFywyzr6gcOAiA7pwhSgXO2nTx6gnZWFhKPbKvWyEhsT%2Fc3ywwN57zEwSr%2FAwg2EAAaDDYzNzQyMzE4MzgwNSIMY2Fg84ozCO4YZcouKtwD0734KX5IiICnCDorUMF2rOK5YpXrOwmxIyuMVkSNecjmY7YL5mM8gE71nSfhhEvIso%2BCq9HZCycY4luZy94aBl%2F3WZEuEa4eDktRqkUm8iVL34l7Oh%2BSInu8e885cvpcpMRtRS%2BxjBI0m4ZTfRvYYkzJf8EZvs5PlQX%2BEL6t0AV%2Fg2wblLeLJdmaiz5%2BJ7SU%2BzcBjLEdOVnHzmS7W2LKINPYc9JOuExMjYMHZyO4j7DVSbHDKFQ6aGmh%2BKJ9sIoF%2B1uc8jsVmxuNyKuXnRbJmi61n%2BsfhA1Ku%2FRwjNiu91v%2FyajMCjNy4jZ0vqoECK99vzLGuMxjgEFA8JnlTYn90FOQaWAm9fkzwmKeSAhtX4QY1DZi2zdTR6GtrMRPbdGPPPzad7rAytj1ZrH%2FpDGvGG