eAomluOqvHlgvkIpfz2zncqQ%2FAdGhIiO7fcMalZpKQYaPeznz5RL%2Bte8jp177T92aduXzPUjLH98qIoCX26oR4t3cpUzFvGdXNh3I%2FkqJYuqmhpp3li3fdQY%2BW%2BleB2s8eem%2FtXie7bLmd0xVgn&X-Amz-Signature=9351a326a7f1e0388bd638525057eb2a0cb859fc4d4ef3f904c20aa82ecce1ab&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&x-amz-checksum-mode=ENABLED&x-id=GetObject)\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n# **The Boy & the Bear**\n\n\n**Passport description:** “The aesthetic interior of The Boy & the Bear is as stunning as their coffee. Their drink menu and shop highlight Colombian culture and the best of Colombian coffee”\n\n\n**Passport benefit:** 15% off\n\n\nI went here with my Caltech bestie, Kayane Dingilian. She ordered an Iced Caramel Macciato and I ordered a Mocha Late. I truly love Colombian coffee, so this was a solid drink. Very enjoyable. What surprised me, though, was how good the pastries were! They looked a little burnt, so I wasn’t expecting anything amazing. Kayane and I both ordered a Tomato, Parmesan, and Cashew Pesto Croissant. It was delectable! Weeks later, I am still thinking about this croissant. It was SO good. I miss it. I’ll be back again for it.\n \n \n\n\n![Interior of the Boy & the Bear (photo cred: Victoria Davis).](https://prod-files-secure.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/c265dfb9-8ac9-4320-8eb7-2a303d3ca597/b5b5c669-1f1a-4d4c-8260-b61f2aaf0d62/Boy001.jpg?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Credential=ASIAZI2LB466W4UPY42I%2F20260104%2Fus-west-2%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260104T205418Z&X-Amz-Expires=3600&X-Amz-Security-Token=IQoJb3JpZ2luX2VjEG0aCXVzLXdlc3QtMiJHMEUCIA3Q5TuBGOEbHo9DK27kW7o%2F2vBHbJDl8A%2F8SfmuxSoUAiEAw77WO1KYHuLL3y098Z3zWFc0md%2BUYkTGRTCFOR8g9MMq%2FwMINhAAGgw2Mzc0MjMxODM4MDUiDCeeJKOL%2B78SXchgHSrcA46fEmNwxudN27UDh25a7s6%2BICHDf%2FUQ%2BhSXyIkcS1lM2ouJBa%2FmJQ%2FEtSCE4%2B%2FsvFuLd22NMtYavuwlGyStt6r8caLPK2ccf3F2l%2BPSzQrl30Vhx%2F5QQGjnK%2FMpE9%2BG5%2Boi8dpD3ULaW870gF2GzevLcyCD6uHTwSLdXFqid0tgKGaEG6tjUx8uguCXjfieE2Qc9Koi2R7Ik%2BO8%2FsXFTDtaQHgunPm3B0yL6%2Bj%