ns, or changes that may have occurred post-2005.\n\n\nNow that we measured Caltech; MIT being 2.3x larger than Caltech. It would take 197,800,000,000 grapes to fill up MIT. \n\n\nSo there you have it! Nearly 198 billion grapes are needed to fill out the Massachusetts Institute of Technology! Using Caltech’s data in 2005 of course. Get rekt!\n\n	2025-10-30 03:30:00+00	6cc3888f-d9fa-4075-add9-b596e6fc44f3	6cc3888f-d9fa-4075-add9-b596e6fc44f3
