ory committee also met with college board?\n\n\n    so did ssawg – college board treats scores of 750 vs 800 as essentially the same student statistically speaking, especially on the scale of 200 students (caltech)\n\n\n    [jowilliams@collegeboard.org](mailto:jowilliams@collegeboard.org) \n\n\nJan 5 - ssawg presented to faculty admissions committee (leadbetter et al) and faculty athletics committee + ashley + betsy (SAT slides + preliminary student athlete report)\n\n\nJan 8 – first version of petition (8 profs – are any on the admissions committee?)\n\n\nJan 16 – final petition\n\n\nit was a coincidence that harvard announce on the same day (jacob has heard many people say ‘we got lucky’)\n\n\nour biggest questions\n\n1. How did this change get pushed through?\n\n    it seems like the faculty pushed it through, despite the desires of admissions\n\n	2025-11-08 19:42:00+00	6cc3888f-d9fa-4075-add9-b596e6fc44f3	6cc3888f-d9fa-4075-add9-b596e6fc44f3
